         {
          "h_title": "Understanding Doodle Generations",
          "main_title": "The pet store with the largest variety of puppy breeds in Singapore!",
          "author": null,
          "language": "en",
          "level": 2,
          "primary_content": [
           {
            "text": "Doodle generations describe how a doodle dog is bred. The letters and numbers (F1, F1B, F2, etc.) simply explain which parents were used in the breeding. Most doodles come from crossing a Poodle with another breed such as a Golden Retriever to produce a Goldendoodle. Each generation changes the genetic mix slightly, which can influence coat type, shedding level, and predictability. F1 Doodle 50% Poodle + 50% Retriever An F1 doodle is the first cross between two purebred dogs.",
            "url": null,
